# Nothing recorded from a real vehicle belongs in this repository.
#
# This repo is PUBLIC. A session CSV is not an abstract dataset: it is a
# timestamped record of every trip its owner took -- when they left, when they
# arrived, how fast they drove, how hard they braked and cornered -- tied to a
# named account. No coordinates are needed for that to be a personal activity
# log, and 58 sessions covering five days were published here before anyone
# noticed. That is the mistake this file exists to make unrepeatable.
#
# The rule is deny-by-default: everything under evidence/ is ignored, and an
# exception has to be added deliberately for anything that is genuinely not
# personal. That way a fresh clone protects its owner without them having to
# know any of this, which is the only kind of protection that works.
*

# ...except the rules themselves.
!.gitignore
